# Dampfer: the paddle steamer "Kaiser Franz Josef I." (1873), side view,
# bow on the right (moving platform, D-077, one-way waiting ride). Hull:
# white bulwark w/i with b/s saloon windows over an o gilt band and a dark
# d/m hull, k outline, gilt scrolls o/Y at bow and stern. Amidships the
# half-round paddle box (x 63-96, rows 19-31, no flat top) in w/i with o
# gilt rays round a Y/o hub; below the deck the red r/R paddles (the
# hazard) turn in a k-framed B opening at the waterline (rays and paddles
# step 15 deg per ride frame; 2 px floats on rows 45-46). One thin funnel
# Y/o/O with a d top band under a k flare, x 70-77, and no smoke (diesel
# since 1954). The wheelhouse at the bow: windows on two posts, open below
# (the skipper inside: B cap, w shirt), under a pointed O/l roof (apex
# row 12, 20 px above the deck). 1 px i railings, a few passengers (one waving), an r/w
# lifebuoy, and at the stern a staff with the r/w/r flag (limp in idle,
# fluttering in ride).
#
# Walking surface: row 32 (k edge, w cap-rail lip at row 33) across all
# 160 px; the hitbox is the 160x16 body (rows 32-47, bottom = waterline).
# Built with a throwaway script, frozen here; the grids are the source.
sprite = dampfer
size   = 160x48
origin = 80,48
hitbox = 0,32,160,16
anim   = idle frames=1
anim   = ride frames=2 ticks=8 loop
